    {
      "id": "p0196-b013",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Although this line seems to be inaccessible through normal play, the translator localized it into Japanese for completeness' sake. In this case, the translator replaced the phrase \"hang out\" with tanomi no tsww, which literally means \"a rope of reliance\", but functionally means \"a mainstay\" or \"something you can depend on\". Thus the final Japanese line drops the invitation and instead roughly says \"Hehe ... Hehehe ... I'm a real reliable 'lifeline', y'know?\".",
